{# The line table on a purchase document's VIEW screen — the buy-side twin of
   sales_detail_line_table.html.twig, and the fix for the same defect that file records: PO's
   "Lines" table and VendorBill's "Lines" table were two independently hand-rolled tables of
   almost the same columns, reading almost the same accessors, and this is the one file both now
   render through.

   Unlike the sell side's three line entities, PurchaseOrderLine and VendorBillLine do not share a
   common interface — but they share enough accessor NAMES (getName/getSku/getVendorSku/
   getUnitCost/getSubtotal/getTaxCode, and now getWeight/getBatch/getDisplayUnitLabel/
   getDisplayUnitCost/getBaseUnitLabel/getQuantityEntered/getUnitOfMeasure — #full-parity,
   2026-09-13) that this partial reads real entities directly, exactly as
   sales_detail_line_table.html.twig does, and needs no flat-hash normalisation step. The one place
   they genuinely differ is quantity: PurchaseOrderLine states Ordered/Received/Outstanding (a
   fulfillment history), VendorBillLine a single Quantity (what was charged). That is handled the
   same way `showBatch` handles the sell side's one real column difference — a boolean, not a
   branch on which document this is. Batch and U/M/Weight are NOT such a difference here: both
   PurchaseOrderLine and VendorBillLine carry all three identically, so unlike the sell side's
   `showBatch` flag those columns are simply always rendered.

   What is NOT here, same reasons as the sell side's file:

     The <section>, its heading and its padding — each screen keeps its own chrome.

     The totals. VendorBill carries them as this table's own <tfoot> (mirroring Invoice); PurchaseOrder
     carries a box beside the table (mirroring Order). `footTemplate` is a path, not parameters,
     for the same reason: a dozen conditional money rows is not a value.

   Parameters
   ----------
   lines            required  the document's line ENTITIES, in sortOrder.
   perLineTax       required  per-line tax amounts, positional. Pass [] for none.
   perLineTaxLabel  required  per-line tax code LABELS, positional. Pass [] for none.
   emptyMessage     required  what the empty row says. Each document names itself.
   tableStyle       required  the <table> element's inline style — VendorBill collapses its
                              borders because it carries a foot; PurchaseOrder does not.
   feeRows          optional  the MAIN-LINE freight/fee rows to list beside the products, already
                              filtered by the caller, each {label, amount}. Defaults to [].
   showFulfillment  optional  true to carry Ordered/Received/Outstanding instead of a single
                              Quantity column — PurchaseOrder passes it, VendorBill does not.
                              Defaults to false.
   currency         optional  prefixed onto every money cell, e.g. "CAD 12.34". Empty renders a
                              bare `$`.
   footTemplate     optional  a <tfoot> to render inside this table, as a template path — only
                              VendorBill has one. `columns` is added to its context automatically.
   footContext      optional  what `footTemplate` is rendered with.
#}
{% set fulfillment = showFulfillment|default(false) %}
{% set money = currency|default('') ? currency ~ ' ' : '$' %}
{% set columns = [
    {label: 'Description'},
    {label: 'Our SKU'},
    {label: 'Their Part No.'},
    {label: 'Weight'},
    {label: 'U/M'},
]|merge(fulfillment ? [
    {label: 'Ordered', align: 'right'},
    {label: 'Received', align: 'right'},
    {label: 'Outstanding', align: 'right'},
] : [
    {label: 'Quantity', align: 'center'},
])|merge([
    {label: 'Unit Cost', align: 'right'},
    {label: 'Subtotal', align: 'right'},
    {label: 'Tax Code'},
    {label: 'Tax $', align: 'right'},
    {label: 'Batch'},
]) %}

<div class="wide-table-wrap">
    <table class="admin-grid-table" style="{{ tableStyle }}">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                {% for column in columns %}
                    <th{% if column.align is defined %} style="text-align:{{ column.align }};"{% endif %}>{{ column.label }}</th>
                {% endfor %}
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for line in lines %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ line.name }}</td>
                    <td>{{ line.sku|default('') ?: '—' }}</td>
                    <td>{{ line.vendorSku|default('') ?: '—' }}</td>
                    <td>{{ line.weight|default('') ?: '—' }}</td>
                    <td>{{ line.displayUnitLabel }}</td>
                    {% if fulfillment %}
                        {# Ordered/Received/Outstanding are all base-unit figures — receiving and the
                           outstanding balance are inherently counted in the base unit — so the
                           entered-unit expression is a hint under Ordered rather than the primary
                           figure, the inverse of the plain Quantity column below (#full-parity,
                           2026-09-13). #}
                        <td style="text-align:right;">{{ line.quantityOrdered|qty }}{% if line.unitOfMeasure %}<br><small style="color:#94a3b8;">= {{ line.quantityEntered|qty }} {{ line.displayUnitLabel }}</small>{% endif %}</td>
                        <td style="text-align:right;">{{ line.quantityReceived|qty }}{% if line.overReceived %} <strong>(over)</strong>{% endif %}</td>
                        <td style="text-align:right;">{{ line.quantityOutstanding|qty }}</td>
                    {% else %}
                        <td style="text-align:center;">{{ line.quantityEntered|qty }}{% if line.unitOfMeasure %}<br><small style="color:#94a3b8;">= {{ line.quantity|qty }} {{ line.baseUnitLabel }}</small>{% endif %}</td>
                    {% endif %}
                    <td style="text-align:right;">{{ money }}{{ line.displayUnitCost|price }}</td>
                    <td class="po-line-subtotal" style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ money }}{{ line.subtotal|amount }}</strong></td>
                    <td>{{ perLineTaxLabel[loop.index0]|default((line.taxCode|default('')) ?: 'E') }}</td>
                    <td class="po-line-tax" style="text-align:right;">{{ money }}{{ perLineTax[loop.index0]|default(0)|amount }}</td>
                    <td class="po-batch-cell">{{ line.batch|default('') ?: '—' }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% else %}
                <tr><td colspan="{{ columns|length }}" class="empty-table-cell"><span>{{ emptyMessage }}</span></td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
            {# A main-line freight/fee charge is a LINE ITEM by design, so it is a row of this
               table beside the products — the buy-side mirror of the sell side's own fee rows. #}
            {% for feeRow in feeRows|default([]) %}
                <tr class="fee-line-row">
                    <td><strong>{{ feeRow.label }}</strong></td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    {% if fulfillment %}
                        <td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td>
                    {% else %}
                        <td style="text-align:center;">—</td>
                    {% endif %}
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ money }}{{ feeRow.amount|amount }}</strong></td>
                    <td>{{ feeRow.taxClass|default('') ?: '—' }}</td>
                    <td style="text-align:right;">{{ feeRow.tax is defined ? money ~ feeRow.tax|amount : '—' }}</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
        {% if footTemplate is defined and footTemplate is not null %}
            {% include footTemplate with footContext|default({})|merge({columns: columns|length}) only %}
        {% endif %}
    </table>
</div>
